.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T14:59:19-08:00","id":1287688,"title":"","content":"Hopefully criminal charges will be laid....this is horrific abuse and rape. I'd like Paradox to shitcan whoever wrote the defence of Zak S after ignoring all the available evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:18:06-08:00","id":1287697,"title":"","content":"Criminal charges are highly unlikely. Depends on when and where things happen precisely there are all sorts of legal hurdles such as statutes of limitation to take into account. The US legal system is generally extremely poor at handling these sorts of cases, and this creates a vicious cycle of the police and prosecutors not wanting to take cases forward when there's so little chance of a conviction.<br /> <br /> The women involved also have to go file charges - a notoriously horrible experience - and see the case through to the end; suffering considerable additional psychological trauma.<br /> <br /> I would love to see charges filed, but I don't have hope for it because I know how much the system is designed against the victims in these sorts of cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T15:36:09-08:00","id":1287712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1286614-zak-s-s-ex-wife-speaks-out?p=1287697#post1287697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Criminal charges are highly unlikely. Depends on when and where things happen precisely there are all sorts of legal hurdles such as statutes of limitation to take into account. The US legal system is generally extremely poor at handling these sorts of cases, and this creates a vicious cycle of the police and prosecutors not wanting to take cases forward when there's so little chance of a conviction.<br /> <br /> The women involved also have to go file charges - a notoriously horrible experience - and see the case through to the end; suffering considerable additional psychological trauma.<br /> <br /> I would love to see charges filed, but I don't have hope for it because I know how much the system is designed against the victims in these sorts of cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup....still.....I can hope. But I wouldn't want the victims to suffer anymore....<br /> <br /> I guess I'll just have to start believing really strongly in karma....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","r